  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project has undergone team expansions, adding five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, as well as Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Key updates include a security protocol enhancement effective January next year, a budget increase for compliance to $55,000, and an approved $15,000 training budget. The team is exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology and is seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November."
